  "question": {
    "text": "The function <math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is defined as&nbsp;<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></math>. From the following statements,<br />\r<br />\rI. <math><mi>f</mi></math> is one-one<br />\r<br />\rII. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is onto<br />\r<br />\rIII. <math><mi>f</mi></math> is a decreasing function<br />\r<br />\rthe true statements are"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "only I, II",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "only II, III",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "only I, III",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "I, II, III",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, <math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>R</mi></math> such that <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> be two elements of <math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> such that <math><msub><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br />Since, if two images are equal, then their elements are equal, therefore it is one-one function.<br /><br />Since, <math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is positive for every value of <math><mi>x</mi></math>, therefore <math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is into.<br /><br />On differentiating w.r.t. <math><mi>x</mi></math>, we get <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></math> for every value of <math><mi>x</mi></math>.<br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo></math> It is decreasing function.<br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo></math> Statement I and III are true."
  }
